# Production site config for the Forkly demo stand.
#
# One Caddy instance serves three sites: the GraphQL API (reverse-proxied to the
# `app` container) and the two Vite frontends (built statically and mounted into
# this container under /srv).
#
# All addresses come from the environment so that the very same file works with
# a real domain (api.forkly.example.com) and, while the brand name is still
# being chosen, with a wildcard-DNS name that resolves to the server IP
# (api.203-0-113-10.sslip.io). Caddy requests a Let's Encrypt certificate for
# every address listed here, which means DNS must already resolve to this server
# before the stack is started - otherwise ACME fails and Caddy retries against
# the rate limit.
#
#   API_ADDRESS    e.g. api.203-0-113-10.sslip.io
#   ADMIN_ADDRESS  e.g. admin.203-0-113-10.sslip.io
#   SITE_ADDRESS   one or more addresses, comma-separated (apex + www),
#                  e.g. "203-0-113-10.sslip.io, www.203-0-113-10.sslip.io"
#
# Select this file with CADDYFILE=Caddyfile.prod (see .env.example). It replaces
# the development Caddyfile, which only proxies the API over plain HTTP.

{$API_ADDRESS} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy app:8000
}

{$ADMIN_ADDRESS} {
	encode gzip
	root * /srv/admin
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}

{$SITE_ADDRESS} {
	encode gzip
	root * /srv/www
	try_files {path} /index.html
	file_server
}
